<package xmlns="http://www.idpf.org/2007/opf" version="3.0" unique-identifier="book-id"><metadata xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><dc:identifier id="book-id">urn:uuid:9f990f02-83b0-45aa-b679-d6862ba2225f</dc:identifier><dc:title>The Arrears Queue</dc:title><dc:creator>James Crutchley</dc:creator><dc:language>en</dc:language><dc:description><![CDATA[There are a hundred ways for a sixteen-year-old girl to disappear in a city full of guilds, placement offices, and Ministry paperwork. Nadia Vess has chosen the most dangerous one: survival by combat.

Her class is worthless on paper. Her body is worse. Every hit she takes is added to a deferred pool of damage that does not resolve immediately. It sits in her, waiting, building toward a later ruin. When the queue exceeds her maximum health, she dies. No downed state. No rescue. No second chance. It is a brutal, impossible mechanic that makes her functionally immortal for a few minutes and doomed the rest of the time.

The only thing keeping her alive is a dungeon the Guild wrote off as empty.

Beneath an abandoned pumping station, in a sealed site that should be dead, a monster still prowls. To everyone else, it is worthless. To Nadia, it is a job. A way to pay for food. A way to keep her name off the files. A way to survive long enough to keep living. The System does not reward her for killing it. It rewards her for holding its attention.

That is the problem. The method is not clean, not legal, and not safe. It is a slow, grinding act of attrition, a battle against both a monster and the damage it leaves behind. Every session costs her more than she can afford. Every missed meal, every exhausted night, every second she spends too long in the dark pushes her closer to the threshold where the debt kills her.

Nadia is not a hero. She is a girl trying to stay alive in a world that only values efficiency, compliance, and measurable output. She is trying to stay in school, stay fed, and stay off the Ministry's radar while she quietly turns a broken class into a source of income. It is a life built on impossible math and bad decisions, and the longer she keeps going, the more dangerous it becomes.

This is not a story about glory. It is a story about survival, hunger, time, and the terrifying cost of staying alive in a world that treats a body like a resource. It is a brutal LitRPG survival tale about a girl with no room to fail, a system built against her, and a future that only gets more expensive the longer she survives.]]></dc:description><meta property="dcterms:modified">2026-08-27T16:32:47Z</meta><meta name="cover" content="cover-image"/></metadata><manifest><item id="nav" href="nav.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml" properties="nav"/><item id="css" href="Styles/book.css" media-type="text/css"/><item id="cover-image" href="Images/cover.jpg" media-type="image/jpeg" properties="cover-image"/><item id="cover-page" href="cover.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="title-page" href="title-page.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="chapter-01" href="Text/chapter-01.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="chapter-02" href="Text/chapter-02.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="chapter-03" href="Text/chapter-03.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="chapter-04" href="Text/chapter-04.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="chapter-05" href="Text/chapter-05.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="chapter-06" href="Text/chapter-06.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="chapter-07" href="Text/chapter-07.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="chapter-08" href="Text/chapter-08.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="chapter-09" href="Text/chapter-09.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="chapter-10" href="Text/chapter-10.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="chapter-11" href="Text/chapter-11.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="chapter-12" href="Text/chapter-12.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/><item id="chapter-13" href="Text/chapter-13.xhtml" media-type="application/xhtm